{{!--
    Renders an AsciiDoc heading at the given absolute level.

    `level` is the absolute heading level (1 = `=`, 2 = `==`, 3 = `===`, ...),
    matching `markup/h.html.hbs`'s convention so consumers pass the same
    number in both formats.

    Parameters:
        - partial block: heading text.
        - level: heading level (1, 2, ...).  Defaults to 1.
        - id:    optional anchor.

    Example:
        {{#> markup/h level=2 id="section-id" }}Section Title{{/markup/h}}

    See: https://mrdocs.com/docs/mrdocs/develop/generators.html#dom_reference
--}}
{{#if id}}[#{{{id}}}]
{{/if}}
{{{repeat "=" (or level 1)}}} {{> @partial-block }}

